Refs #1789 #1790

Fixes QA #1790 blocker **B16**: `deliver_file` was advertised to every Bee but always refused in the default deployment. The Bridge injected its `artifact_delivery` service only when `DIGITALMATE_HIVE_DOCUMENT_FORMAT(S)` was set, and no deploy config sets that.

## Change (scope: only this)
- **Config default.** New `dm_hive_tools/config/delivery.toml` with `formats = ["PDF", "PPTX", "DOCX", "XLSX"]`.
  - The env document formats still override it. They also still turn on document generation; the delivery default does not grant any `create_hive_*` tool.
  - An empty list turns delivery off.
- **Service always present.** Whenever the direct Home is on and a delivery format is configured, the Bridge now creates the private byte owner (`HiveDocumentBytes`), the Home document projection (`configure_documents`) and its erasure. Delivered files therefore show up in the user's Home. `ArtifactDelivery` refuses a file type outside the configured formats.
- **Guard.** `ToolHandler.requires` names the Host service a tool can't run without; `deliver_file` requires `artifact_delivery`. Without that service the tool is:
  - left out of the Host tool specs and journaled names;
  - left out of the Bee rail policy, so the Bee runtime never sees it;
  - refused as "not available";
  - refused before starting even when an effect was already wired.
- `ownership.json`: new public `deliver.delivery_formats` and `hive_bee_runtime.bee_delivery_formats`.

## Tests
- New `temp/hive-tools/tests/test_hive_tools_deliver_config.py` (5) and `tests/test_hive_deliver_file_default.py` (4). All 9 fail on unpatched main. They cover:
  - the default formats and validation of the format list;
  - the tool is neither offered nor callable without the service, and is offered with it;
  - a format outside the configured list is refused;
  - real Bridge composition with Home on and no env: `deliver_file` is offered, documents and erasure are configured, and no generation grant is added;
  - the env override;
  - an empty formats list hides the tool;
  - the rail policy drops `deliver_file` and `send_file_to_user` without the service.
- Updated existing tests that assumed `deliver_file` is always offered (`test_hive_bee_tools`, `test_hive_tools_providers`) so they inject the service. Updated `test_unbound_delivery_refuses` to cover a service lost after wiring.
- Remote 3.13 venv:
  - `temp/hive-tools/tests`: 152 passed.
  - Bridge deliver, Bee-tools, browser-helper, owned-Bee, answer-startup, local-tools, input-sources, workswarm-effects, home-trial, input-PDF and serve-settings suites: green.
  - Architecture scan: 0 findings.
  - The 2 `test_hive_document_model_reads` failures also fail on unmodified main.

Device: QA is already testing delivery with the env set (same service path). The coordinator accepts that run plus these unit tests as evidence.

